; `;@axiom:isr` marks an interrupt entry point, which the hardware
; calls by name with no arguments. A declaration carrying parameters
; contradicts the tag, and the walk has an answer - so it is AX3010
; (axtag-mismatch), not AX3037.
;
; One AX3010, anchored on the declaration: the occurrence is where
; the fix is (remove the parameters, or drop the tag). `plain` is
; the control - the same body without the tag checks clean, proving
; the refusal is the claim and not the code.
(:: tick (-> Int Int))

;@axiom:isr
(fn (tick n) n)

(:: plain (-> Int Int))

(fn (plain n) n)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
